*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Compute the partial derivatives of $f(x, y, z)$ with respect to $x$, $y$, and $z$.
2. Substitute the coordinates of the point $P(1, -1, 2)$ into these partial derivative expressions.
3. Form the gradient vector $nabla f(P) = chevron.l (partial f)/(partial x)(P), (partial f)/(partial y)(P), (partial f)/(partial z)(P) chevron.r$.
